From 8f136278108128b71bd9126cb2e0cc22d2c9b46c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Lindeburg <jonaslindeburg@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:06:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the ASUS Vivobook S14 (S3407QA)

Snapdragon X X1P42100 laptop, derived from the Vivobook S 15 tree:
keyboard and touchpad, Samsung ATNA40KW01 OLED panel, NVMe, two USB-C
ports, USB-A, HDMI through a Parade PS185HDM bridge, WCN6855 Wi-Fi and
Bluetooth, speakers, headset jack and battery.

[birk: Jonas Lindeburg's tree as he published it on 2026-09-13, which
 he runs on Ubuntu with all of the above working; unchanged apart from
 the Makefile entry. Wi-Fi comes up on about three boots in five, the
 microphones capture silence and the webcam doesn't work yet. Firmware
 from qcom/x1p42100/ASUSTeK/vivobook-s14/]
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile             |    1 +
 .../dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s14.dts   | 1285 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 1286 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p42100-asus-vivobook-s14.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
